  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nx = 0.35\n\ny = 6/5\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nThe value of the expression: x × y ÷ (100x - 30y) × (y / 2.1) + 6 / y\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nExpression: x × y ÷ (100x - 30y) × (y / 2.1) + 6 / y\n\n⇒ x = 0.35, y = 6/5 = 1.2\n\n⇒ x × y = 0.35 × 1.2 = 0.42\n\n⇒ 100x = 100 × 0.35 = 35\n\n⇒ 30y = 30 × 1.2 = 36\n\n⇒ 100x - 30y = 35 - 36 = -1\n\n⇒ y / 2.1 = 1.2 / 2.1 = 0.5714\n\n⇒ x × y ÷ (100x - 30y) = 0.42 ÷ -1 = -0.42\n\n⇒ -0.42 × (y / 2.1) = -0.42 × 0.5714 = -0.24\n\n⇒ 6 / y = 6 / 1.2 = 5\n\n⇒ Final value = -0.24 + 5 = 4.76\n\n**∴ The correct answer is option (4).**",
